# route: level=w1_l2_coop difficulty=beginner players=2 ends=exit after=tally expect=hurts:0,wipes:0,eggs:0,x2_gates:2,min_checkpoints:6,min_kills:15
# w1_l2_coop "Canopy Village" for two - Beginner two-stream route proof (designer DB1, wf10; ticks:P1|P2, keys L R U D F K S;
# recorded from closed-loop duo bots, build/db1/p6/bot_w1_l2.gd --dlift2_bottom=1096). The forest floor: P1 opens
# the inset spot, the pot and the crate; the Shellback by the hut by a pincer (P2 baits, P1 jumps over it and clubs
# its back). Gate 'treehouse' (a boost ledge, 8 rows): P2 stands on the root mound by the deck's edge, P1 lands on
# his head holding Up (the Shoulder Hop), steers onto the tree house deck and clubs the coiled vine down from there;
# P2 climbs it. Over the bat gaps (P2 follows once P1 stands beyond a gap) and up the branches; both ride the
# diagonal lift and the trunk lift together (the same keys on the same tick). Gate 'shaft': through the trunk's
# doorway; P2 stands under the ledge 8 rows up, P1 shoulder-hops onto its left cell; P2 walks onto the lift stone,
# P1 crouches on the plate of the ledge's right cell (Down held) and the stone lifts P2 to the ledge; both climb
# the hanging vine to the trunk top. Down the big branch (P1 clubs the Snatcher bat). The village deck: P1 drops
# first, steering left under the branch, and clubs the stinger as it dives; P2 drops once it is dead.
# Both jump over the deck's Shellback on the same tick (no room behind it for a pincer) and drop to the deck below;
# its hopper; the down lift together, left early (some 40 px over the deck, before the near leaper's copy arrives);
# the leaper pits crossed in their pauses, the snapper and the bats of the row-84 deck, the lowest deck's hopper,
# and both into the exit totem. A waiting hero taps Down now and then (no role is idle 243 ticks). Club only, no S.
